  "title": "Constantine the Great",
  "summary": "Constantine the Great, Roman emperor from 306 to 337, was born at Naissus in present-day Serbia. He is said to have converted to Christianity during his 312 campaign against Maxentius. He issued the Edict of Milan, which tolerated all religions, called the Council of Nicaea in 325, and moved the seat of empire to Byzantium, dedicated in 330 as Constantinople.",
